id: pm-github-01n8
title: Allow public technical forms in the tracker privacy gate
description: "Permit only the specified public interfaces, reserved-domain fixtures, git SSH transport, hosted runner workspaces and placeholder home segments; retain concrete host and personal email refusals. Verify inherited tests, exact mutation proof, full eight-repository measurement and unchanged release gates."
type: Issue
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[4]: changelog-unreleased,gate,"gh:unbraind/pm-github#193",privacy
created_at: "2026-11-02T13:12:32.087Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-02T19:46:38.736Z"
author: codex-sol
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Every specified public technical form passes plain, serialized and full tracker scans; concrete host data and non-reserved personal email refusals remain intact; exact removal and broadening mutations pass; eight-repository rule/hash measurement and README boundaries are documented; unchanged release gates pass; branch pushed once without a PR or closing this item."
repro_steps: Run the original embedded issue snippets through scanLineForRuleHits at baseline 9586643 and compare to the public technical forms corpus.
expected_result: Public technical fixtures pass while concrete host and personal data remain refused.
actual_result: "The baseline refuses procfs documentation, reserved-domain fixtures, hosted runner workspaces and placeholder home examples."
component: tracker privacy gate
comments[23]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-02T13:12:47.776Z",codex-sol,"Audited the inherited gate and all three changed existing test files. Existing example.org replacements use non-reserved example.dev and retain refusal semantics. The daily-sync test instead moved two refusal cases into allowances; restore equivalent non-reserved refusals while retaining reserved-domain allow cases. Also verify exact domain boundaries, runner workspace segments, placeholders and traversal before extending proof coverage. No upstream writes beyond the authorized final branch push."
  "2026-11-02T13:18:43.588Z",codex-sol,"Inherited 15-mutation table passed before edits: removal flips procfs 8, reserved emails 10, git transport 4, POSIX runner 2, Windows runner 3, toolcache 1, POSIX placeholders 6, Windows placeholders 3; broadening flips domain anchors 5, POSIX runner 2, Windows runner 2, traversal 5, embedded identity 4, proc shape 3, bracket lead-ins 1. Extended to 19 mutations to observe sysfs, non-git transport local parts and placeholder position. Fixed reserved-domain prefix truncation, added case-insensitive bare localhost coverage, and restored both daily-sync refusal cases with non-reserved example.dev fixtures. Focused tests passed 57/57; proof harness tests passed 4/4. Full release gates remain pending."
  "2026-11-02T13:20:28.315Z",codex-sol,"Eight-repository read-only measurement completed after checking the API floor: 68 issues and 82 comments, all titles/bodies/comments paginated. Current baseline finds 3 absolute-host-path occurrences in pm-review (2 distinct hashes); updated gate finds zero across all eight repos. Original embedded snippets separately show before/after: review 3/0, context 1/0, jev 0/0, rust 1/0, swarm 2/0, ops 2/2. Retained ops findings are deliberate root/temp refusals. Full rule/hash counts and the exact 19-mutation table are in docs/gate-public-forms-evidence.md. Corpus: 43 allow and 50 refuse rows. Proof-script targeted coverage is 100 percent for lines/statements/functions/branches; thresholds unchanged. dist is ignored and untracked, so build output will be regenerated but not committed."
  "2026-11-02T13:26:10.955Z",codex-sol,"The release suite is running with unchanged thresholds and no timeout cap on the shell command. Added required acceptance, estimate and Issue metadata to this item. Adjacent baseline tracker-hygiene warnings from pm validate are recorded on existing maintenance item pm-github-rv9m; no unrelated records were repaired or closed. The proposed tracker change passes runTrackerGate with zero findings."
  "2026-11-02T13:26:27.547Z",codex-sol,"Final exact mutation table (allow-flips are newly refused allow rows; refuse-flips are newly admitted refusal rows). All 19 pass with no unexpected rows:\nok   remove-sysfs-allowance: allow-flips=2 refuse-flips=0\nok   remove-procfs-allowance: allow-flips=8 refuse-flips=0\nok   remove-reserved-domain-allowance: allow-flips=12 refuse-flips=0\nok   remove-git-transport-allowance: allow-flips=4 refuse-flips=0\nok   remove-runner-workspace-posix: allow-flips=2 refuse-flips=0\nok   remove-runner-workspace-windows: allow-flips=3 refuse-flips=0\nok   remove-toolcache-allowance: allow-flips=1 refuse-flips=0\nok   remove-placeholder-home-posix: allow-flips=8 refuse-flips=0\nok   remove-placeholder-home-windows: allow-flips=3 refuse-flips=0\nok   broaden-reserved-domain-anchor: allow-flips=0 refuse-flips=7\nok   broaden-runner-shape-posix: allow-flips=0 refuse-flips=3\nok   broaden-runner-shape-windows: allow-flips=0 refuse-flips=2\nok   broaden-git-transport-local-part: allow-flips=0 refuse-flips=2\nok   broaden-placeholder-position-posix: allow-flips=0 refuse-flips=1\nok   broaden-placeholder-position-windows: allow-flips=0 refuse-flips=1\nok   remove-escape-segment-check: allow-flips=0 refuse-flips=5\nok   remove-embedded-identity-check: allow-flips=0 refuse-flips=4\nok   broaden-proc-shape: allow-flips=0 refuse-flips=3\nok   remove-bracket-leadins: allow-flips=0 refuse-flips=1"
  "2026-11-02T13:47:13.928Z",codex-sol,"PM-linked verification completed successfully: node --test test/gate-public-forms.test.ts test/prove-gate-public-forms.test.ts test/gate.test.ts test/daily-sync-privacy.test.ts test/import-gate.test.ts via pm test pm-github-01n8 --run --progress passed 134/134, zero failed/cancelled/skipped, exit 0 (1618 seconds). The tracker policy disables automatic result recording, so this comment preserves the verified summary without storing raw command output. Full release:check remains active; no failure observed so far."
  "2026-11-02T15:45:50.166Z",codex-sol,"Recovery audit: both requested item JSON reads parse and all inherited refusal assertions remain intact using non-reserved example.dev fixtures. The rv9m edit recorded unrelated pre-existing tracker hygiene warnings during validation; reverting that item and its paired history file only, because maintenance findings are outside this fix. The allowance audit retains exact reserved-domain matching, git transport only, two runner workspace segments, direct-child home placeholders and traversal refusals. Exactly one local item carries the issue tag; open triage PR 211 contains only three other issue items."
  "2026-11-02T15:53:46.012Z",codex-sol,"Recovery checks: TypeScript compiles; both item reads and every history JSONL record parse. All 19 mutation rows pass exactly (43 allow and 50 refuse corpus rows). The first recovery release run was intentionally stopped after discovering that an in-repository scratch root lets PM fixture initialization discover the parent Git repository. Removed only its generated ignore/attribute additions and scratch directory. Restarted unchanged release:check with a dedicated external scratch directory and guaranteed cleanup; this setup correction changes no source or thresholds."
  "2026-11-02T15:55:26.783Z",codex-sol,"Read-only eight-repository measurement refreshed at 15:53Z: core quota 2349 before and 2152 after, checked before each API page and never below 1500. Fully paginated 68 issue titles/bodies and 82 issue comments, excluding PRs. Every rule/SHA-256 occurrence count reproduces docs/gate-public-forms-evidence.md: current pm-review 3 to 0, all seven other current corpora 0 to 0. Original embedded excerpts separately remain review 3/0, context 1/0, jev 0/0, rust 1/0, swarm 2/0, ops 2/2, vcs 0/0, changelog 0/0. The two remaining excerpt hashes represent intentional root/temp refusals. No matched text was printed or persisted in evidence; measurement scratch directories were removed."
  "2026-11-02T16:17:25.809Z",codex-sol,"The recovery PM-linked command reached its stored 1800-second timeout after 125 passing tests, zero assertion failures and one interrupted file; this is incomplete evidence, not a pass. Increasing only that linked command timeout to 7200 seconds and rerunning the same command with an owned external scratch root. No test, assertion, coverage threshold or release gate is removed or weakened. The full release check continues separately."
  "2026-11-02T16:20:39.418Z",codex-sol,"The same PM-linked regression command is rerunning with a 7200-second timeout and a dedicated external scratch root. Independently matched the interrupted fixture archive's compiled gate SHA-256 to this candidate, then removed its two owned leftover directories; older and unrelated scratch directories were preserved. Both active gate wrappers clean their own scratch roots on completion. Full release verification remains active with no reported assertion failures."
  "2026-11-02T16:37:39.164Z",codex-sol,"Release verification continues with unchanged source and thresholds: 401 passing top-level test lines so far, no reported assertion failures, 111 GB root free. The same linked regression command is also active under the extended timeout. Compilation, docstrings (268 declarations), lint, duplication and the pre-test all-object privacy audit have passed; exact all-source coverage, audit/pack, final changelog verification and attestation remain uncredited until the release command completes."
  "2026-11-02T16:58:36.372Z",codex-sol,"Recovery PM-linked rerun PASSED: the unchanged command ran all 134 tests with 134 passes, zero failures/cancellations/skips and exit 0 (2358 seconds). The earlier 1800-second timeout is superseded by this complete result; the linked timeout is 7200 seconds. The wrapper removed its dedicated scratch root. Full release:check remains active with 438 passing top-level test lines and no reported failures; no final coverage claim yet."
  "2026-11-02T17:10:19.587Z",codex-sol,"Additional recovery audit passed: pm history verification with strict exit validated all 22 then-current records, chain/replay, and equality of the latest after-hash with the current item hash. The full release command remains active, now with 494 passing top-level test lines and no reported failures. The free-space floor remains satisfied; source and assertions are unchanged. Completed 134/134 linked regression evidence remains valid."
  "2026-11-02T17:33:11.356Z",codex-sol,"A focused coverage diagnostic passed 55/55 gate/corpus tests with zero failures/cancellations/skips and found no uncovered branches in the added allowance-helper range. This diagnostic is not a package-wide coverage claim; the unchanged full release check remains active and its exact all-source result is still pending. No source, assertion or threshold changes followed the diagnostic."
  "2026-11-02T17:53:14.188Z",codex-sol,"The first complete recovery suite reported 1607/1609 passes and two assertion failures, zero cancellations/skips. Both are in scope: daily-sync-idempotency still used a reserved example.invalid address as its refusal fixture, and the isolated minimum-SDK source witness omitted the shared corpus imported by the new proof script. Replaced only the refusal address with non-reserved example.dev, preserving every refusal and zero-write assertion. Added the actual corpus dependency to the minimum-SDK source witness; every production/operational module and shipped declaration still type-checks, with no exemption or assertion removed. Linking and running both affected files before repeating the unchanged full release gate."
  "2026-11-02T18:04:24.547Z",codex-sol,"The release command also hit c8 heap exhaustion at the configured 12 GiB limit after the test summary, so it produced no complete coverage receipt. This direct gate blocker is recorded on existing follow-up pm-github-vhi6, which remains open; unlike the unrelated rv9m hygiene edit, this evidence explains the required verification environment. Running a bounded 16 GiB saved-receipt diagnostic before repeating the full release command with a resource-only override. Source inventory, all tests and four 100-percent thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-11-02T18:25:46.307Z",codex-sol,"The saved raw coverage report passed exact 100/100/100/100 at 16 GiB across 29 modules (13776 lines/statements, 437 functions, 5184 branches, zero skips). The targeted fixture retry passed the three daily-sync cases but its minimum-SDK npm install timed out before compilation. Normal npm ping reproduced the transport timeout; both disabling family autoselection and allowing 5000 ms family attempts reached the official registry. The minimum-SDK fixture now offers a validated opt-in transport timer while still clearing inherited Node flags and credentials; its floor, declarations, source-module and runtime assertions are unchanged. Retrying all four affected tests before the full gate."
  "2026-11-02T18:29:47.575Z",codex-sol,"The repaired daily-sync and minimum-SDK files now pass all 4 tests with zero failures, cancellations or skips through the PM-linked command. The exact declared published SDK was installed, all authored production/operational modules plus shipped declarations compiled, and the installed-artifact runtime witness passed. A validated 5000 ms family-attempt timer was used for the real registry transport. The prior 134-test linked result remains valid; product gate code, corpus and mutation table are unchanged. Repeating the full release command with the same 29-source inventory and four exact 100-percent thresholds, using a bounded heap override after the 16 GiB saved-receipt report succeeded."
  "2026-11-02T18:34:56.470Z",codex-sol,"Final full release retry started with NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG=/dev/null, NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size-percentage=55 --network-family-autoselection-attempt-timeout=5000, and PM_GITHUB_TEST_NETWORK_ATTEMPT_TIMEOUT_MS=5000. The percentage override takes precedence over the fixed reporter cap; the effective local heap limit was verified at 17805 MiB. This retains every test, all 29 authored modules and four exact 100-percent thresholds. Real production audit preflight passed with zero vulnerabilities. The new full run uses an owned external scratch root with automatic cleanup; no cached test success is substituted for execution."
  "2026-11-02T19:13:08.966Z",codex-sol,"The fresh final release run continues with 527 passing top-level test lines and no reported failures. The repaired files already passed their separate 4/4 real-consumer check, and no source or assertion changed after that success. All free-space checks remain above the required floor. The pending result is the complete fresh release command, not the prior saved-receipt diagnostic."
  "2026-11-02T19:41:17.610Z",codex-sol,"The fresh complete release:check PASSED, exit 0: 1609/1609 tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips; all 29 authored modules at exact 13776/13776 lines/statements, 437/437 functions and 5184/5184 branches, zero skipped source. Docstrings 268 declarations; zero duplication at unchanged 50-token threshold; privacy 7982 objects with zero findings; production audit zero vulnerabilities; pack dry-run 75 files; canonical changelog check and publish-provenance attestation passed. This is fresh execution with the documented process-local heap/transport profile, not substituted cached test success. Owned release scratch cleanup completed. Final complete SDK read found 162 items and only this #193 owner; PR 211 remains open at 56a20d4 and its tags are only #197/#199/#202. Adding the explicit pending changelog tag without closing this issue."
  "2026-11-02T19:46:37.893Z",codex-sol,"Canonical changelog regeneration and consistency check passed; the only changelog addition is this pending fix under Unreleased. Final diff audit confirms all five edited existing test files retain their original refusal, zero-write, SDK-floor, declaration and runtime assertions; reserved fixtures were replaced with non-reserved example.dev only where refusal is required. The rv9m item/history pair is byte-identical to HEAD. The related vhi6 changes contain only the required gate-memory follow-up evidence and remain open. Verification is complete; releasing this claim before the single combined commit and branch push, without closing the item."
